From 371669e1a5244aebf3df67c77b62db31a6ee1eb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virgil724 <108603174+virgil724@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:02:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ramips: mt7621: add support for Arcadyan WE410443-TC
 (Chunghwa Telecom)

Chunghwa Telecom variant of the Arcadyan WE410443 mesh extender.
Same SoC/radios as the upstream WE410443 (MT7621AT, 128MB RAM,
2x MT7615N) but with 16MB SPI NOR and a dual-image stock layout.

- Flash: 16MB SPI NOR; OpenWrt uses stock "Kernel" slot 0
  (0x50000, 0x7b0000). "Kernel2" slot at 0x810000 is left untouched.
- Stock U-Boot 1.1.3 boots a plain uImage; use uimage-lzma-loader.
- MAC: binary at factory 0xfff0 (LAN +0, 2.4G +1, 5G +2).
- WiFi EEPROM: factory 0x0 (2.4G) and 0x8000 (5G).
- Buttons: WPS GPIO 3, reset GPIO 18 (verified on device).
- Image trimmed for dumb-AP use (no firewall/ppp/ipv6 dhcp) to leave
  768K jffs2 overlay.

Install from stock shell (ssh cht@...):
  mtd_debug erase /dev/mtd4 0 8060928
  mtd_debug write /dev/mtd4 0 <size> sysupgrade.bin

Tested: boot, cold boot, settings persistence, both radios, MACs,
buttons, sysupgrade -T.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
